---
title: "Citation coverage"
description: "A focused corpus document that exercises the .bib rendering fixes: LaTeX accents, corporate authors, @string macros, @incollection/@inproceedings booktitle+pages, paren-delimited entries, manual-References de-duplication, `\\url{}` unwrapping, quoted-brace authors, and special-character cite keys."
date: 2026-06-27
categories:
  - meta
bibliography: [references.bib]
---

This document pins the citation/bibliography rendering fixes. Each paragraph cites
an entry that exercises one fix, and the page supplies its own `# References`
heading so the auto-generated list must render under it (no duplicate heading).

Kernel methods were popularised by a line of work surveyed in
[@muller2018kernel]; the surname accents (`M{\"u}ller`, `Sch{\"o}lkopf`) must
render as Unicode.

The random-graph model of [@erdos1959random] uses the Hungarian double-acute
accent (`Erd{\H{o}}s`), which must compose to "Erdős".

Air-quality limits are set by a corporate author [@who2021guidelines]: a
brace-protected name must render whole, never initialised to "W. H. Organization".

The `@string` macro `springer` is referenced by both a book [@bishop2006pattern]
and a book chapter [@bengio2012practical]; the chapter is an `@incollection`, so
its `booktitle` and `pages` must appear.

An online source [@wiki2025anova] carries its link as a `\url{...}` macro in
`howpublished`; the macro must unwrap to a bare URL (underscores intact), never leak
a backslash.

A quoted single-brace author `"{Ada Lovelace}"` [@lovelace1843notes] is an ordinary
(case-protected) person, so it must initialise to "A. Lovelace", not render whole.

A citation whose key carries a dot [@smith.2020a] must resolve rather than truncate at
the `.` — the reference parser and the `.bib` parser share one key charset.

The transformer paper [@vaswani2017attention] is an `@inproceedings` written with
`(...)` delimiters: its `booktitle` (proceedings) and `pages` must render, and the
paren delimiters must close the entry so the next entry is not cascade-dropped.

That next entry [@lecun1998gradient] must still resolve — a regression in the
paren-delimited close would swallow every following reference.

